<article-title>Development and validation of a geriatric depression screening scale: a preliminary report</article-title><source>J Psychiatr Res</source><volume>17</volume><fpage>37</fpage><lpage>49</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7183759</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b27-cia-0102-189"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yudina</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name></person-group><year>1993</year><article-title>Health is a category of the economy. Moscow</article-title><source>Delavoy Mir</source>March 4, <fpage>16</fpage></citation></ref></ref-list><sec sec-type="display-objects"><title>Tables</title><table-wrap id="t1-cia-0102-189" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Functional Evaluation Framework</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th valign="middle" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>Function</bold></th><th valign="middle" align="left" colspan="3" rowspan="1"><bold>Modifiers of function</bold></th></tr><tr><th colspan="4" rowspan="1"><hr/></th></tr><tr><th valign="middle" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><th valign="middle" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>Ability</bold></th><th valign="middle" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>Motivation</bold></th><th valign="middle" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>Opportunities</bold></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="2" colspan="1"><bold>Functional Status</bold><break/><xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn1-cia-0102-189">*</xref>Physical functioning<break/><xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn1-cia-0102-189">*</xref>Social functioning<break/><break/>Tasks<break/>BADL: Bathing<break/>Dressing<break/>Continence<break/>IADL: Shopping<break/>Handling finances<break/>Food preparation<break/>Housekeeping<break/>Using transportation<break/>AADL: Employment<break/>Participating in political and social activities</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>Physical</bold><break/><xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn1-cia-0102-189">*</xref>Absence of: Disease (acute or chronic)<break/>Disability (congenital or acquired)<break/><xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn1-cia-0102-189">*</xref>Physical maneuvers<break/>Lung function<break/><xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn1-cia-0102-189">*</xref>Bodily pain<break/>Height, weight, blood pressure</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="2" colspan="1"><bold>Psychological</bold><break/><xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn1-cia-0102-189">*</xref>Depression<break/>Sad mood &#x00026; pessimistic outlook<break/>Lack of mental &#x00026; physical energy<break/>Positive or happy mood<break/>Agitation or restlessness<break/>Social withdrawal<break/><xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn1-cia-0102-189">*</xref>Vitality<break/>Efficacy<break/><xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn1-cia-0102-189">*</xref>Religiosity<break/><xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn1-cia-0102-189">*</xref>Perceived role limitations attributed to emotional problems<break/><xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn1-cia-0102-189">*</xref>Perceived role limitations attributed to physical problems</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>Individual</bold><break/><xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn1-cia-0102-189">*</xref>Demographics: Age, education, gender, marital status, nationality, race, number of children<break/><xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn1-cia-0102-189">*</xref>Health habits/life styles: nutrition, alcohol, tobacco, and medication use, vaccinations<break/>Social support<break/>Family structure<break/><xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn1-cia-0102-189">*</xref>Income: Internal and external adequacy of living quarters</td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>Psychological</bold><break/>Absence of: Disease (acute or chronic)<break/>Disability (congenital or acquired)<break/><xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn1-cia-0102-189">*</xref>Cognitive function: Orientations, memory and recall, attention &#x00026; calculation, language ability, and health information knowledge<break/><xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn1-cia-0102-189">*</xref>Mental health<break/><xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn1-cia-0102-189">*</xref>General health perception</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>Societal</bold><break/>Cross-cultural differences: Social support networks<break/><xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn1-cia-0102-189">*</xref>Resources, provision and access to healthcare<break/>Cultural values/religion and politics<break/>Environmental pollution</td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="left" colspan="4" rowspan="1"><bold>Measurements</bold></td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="2" colspan="1">Part of MOS<break/>Physical functioning<break/>Social functioning<break/><break/><break/>Activities of daily living questions: BADL, IADL, AADL</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Part of MOS:<break/>Bodily pain<break/>Problem list of medical diagnoses and disabilities<break/>Measurement of peak flow<break/>Physical maneuvers assessment<break/>Physical measurements</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="2" colspan="1">Part of MOS:<break/>Role limitations physical and emotional and vitality<break/>Yesavage GDS<break/>Political efficacy questions<break/>Religiosity questions</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="2" colspan="1">Demographic data<break/>Vaccination questions<break/>Alcohol and tobacco questions<break/>Social support questions<break/>Hunger questions<break/>Income questions<break/>Home ownership questions<break/>Medication list<break/>Description of living quarters questions<break/>Living quarters safety questions<break/>Social support network questions<break/>Access to healthcare questions<break/>Air quality measures by site</td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Part of MOS: Mental health and general health<break/>Problem list of psychological dia